id: pm-wa39rl
title: "Completed-task transcripts require terminal success, exclusive refusal metadata, and complete recovery"
description: "Greptile and CodeRabbit exact-head review on PR #1133 found that the public transcript parser can accept a task ending in refusal, successful steps can carry refusal-only metadata, and the retry-option fixture lacks its recovery_for edge. Enforce terminal-success topology and mutually exclusive refusal/recovery metadata in the SDK contract and replay corpus."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:contracts","area:sdk",recovery,review-feedback,testing
created_at: "2026-08-27T20:29:24.256Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T05:50:10.852Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T05:50:10.171Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T05:50:10.171Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Every completed task terminates in a non-refusal output; successful outputs reject refusal-only metadata; every corrected retry binds to the refusal it recovers; adversarial parser and replay regressions pass
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Enforced complete transcript recovery topology and reconciled review lifecycles, with typed verification edges connecting every explicitly cited correction owner."
expected_result: "The public SDK transcript contract cannot represent an unsuccessfully terminated completed task or contradictory refusal metadata, and its reviewed correction evidence is represented by matching typed graph relationships."
actual_result: "Transcript invariants remain fully enforced; the final review lifecycle is append-only and all three explicitly cited correction owners are connected by verifies edges. Exact graph composition now passes with 1,342 prose-edge gaps against the immutable 1,343 ceiling."
component: sdk-output-contracts
