  pm-wanwyc,verifies,"2026-08-28T05:49:37.364Z","harness:codex","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T20:29:24.256Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for terminal refusal completion, refusal metadata on successful transcripts, and retry recovery binding found the canonical pm-f05lsg/pm-8pnj lineage plus closed precursor pm-o360q6, but no item covering this combined terminal-topology recurrence. Review sources: Greptile and CodeRabbit on PR #1133 head baae93c."
  "2026-08-27T21:13:27.651Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-27: focused parser/error-guidance/replay suite passed 74/74 tests. Repository exact coverage passed 8,067/8,067 tests with statements 59,914/59,914, branches 45,102/45,102, functions 12,459/12,459, and lines 57,696/57,696. The versioned replay passes five completed tasks, 14 steps, two executable retries, and a 4,349-token composite ceiling at digest sha256:0eeb3296a4bcd5edeb13f6488ae0ebc806adc96b6caa89d87a0f528d37af5c4e."
  "2026-08-27T21:22:06.939Z","harness:codex","Exact-head recurrence 2026-08-27 (Greptile review thread PRRT_kwDORSgRDc6c-7LC): verified valid. Terminal-success alone does not prove recovery closure because an earlier refusal can be followed by an unrelated success without recovery_for. Extend the existing terminal-recovery issue, rather than creating a duplicate, so every refusal in a completed task must have a later successful recovery edge; add the missing adversarial parser case and rerun replay plus exact coverage."
  "2026-08-27T21:31:37.739Z","harness:codex","Final recurrence evidence 2026-08-27: the parser now rejects any completed task containing an unrecovered refusal, even when an unrelated successful step terminates the transcript. The PM-linked focused suite passed 74/74 tests after this change; repository exact coverage passed 8,067/8,067 tests with statements 59,920/59,920, branches 45,108/45,108, functions 12,461/12,461, and lines 57,702/57,702."
  "2026-08-27T21:44:17.171Z","harness:codex","Implementation note: the valid refusal-recovery recurrence exposed an architectural bundling issue: SDK-only transcript parsing currently shares src/sdk/output-contracts.ts with every CLI output envelope. Split the transcript contract behind the aggregate SDK entrypoint, preserve the public surface, and prove the CLI transport floor before re-closing."
  "2026-08-27T22:07:24.312Z","harness:codex","Final architecture evidence 2026-08-28: the transcript parser is isolated under src/sdk/agent while remaining exported from both @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk and @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/contracts. The public surface snapshot reports zero classified changes; 10 SDK entrypoint budgets and all six CLI transport-floor operations pass. Static quality reports 567/567 source docstrings, 4,507/4,507 exported docstrings, 8,184/8,184 member docstrings, zero directory-load/complexity/duplication/import-boundary violations. Exact repository coverage passed 8,067/8,067 tests with statements 59,918/59,918, branches 45,110/45,110, functions 12,461/12,461, and lines 57,700/57,700."
  "2026-08-27T22:46:12.254Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence (CodeRabbit PR #1133 thread PRRT_kwDORSgRDc6c_DrI): transcript args now preserve every validated non-empty token exactly, including leading and trailing whitespace, while ids, descriptions, recovery links, and required-field paths retain normalized semantics. The public contract documents exact preservation and the parser test asserts the literal token \"  triage  \". Linked test passed 74/74; full repository coverage passed 585 files and 8067 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (59919 statements, 45114 branches, 12461 functions, 57701 lines). SDK entrypoint budgets passed all 10 entrypoints and CLI transport floors passed all 6 operations."
  "2026-08-27T22:53:19.830Z","harness:codex","Final public SDK acceptance proof before closure: the built dist/sdk/index.js parser consumed a real transcript in the temporary-workspace acceptance run and returned the argument token \"  literal-filter  \" byte-for-byte, while the CLI black-box refusal remained safe across an explicit -- boundary. The temporary workspace was then removed."
  "2026-08-28T03:22:26.322Z","harness:codex","Review wording correction: the changelog is generated from PM titles. Updated this canonical title to state the implemented behavior: completed transcripts require terminal success, mutually exclusive refusal metadata, and an explicit later successful recovery for every refusal. No implementation or historical evidence changed."
  "2026-08-28T05:09:45.737Z","harness:codex","Append-only lifecycle reconciliation: CodeRabbit correctly identified the historical sequence at indices 16-20 where resolution was written after release and the item was reopened before a fresh claim. This ownership interval records the immutable mismatch explicitly and will end with evidence, close, and release in the correct order; tracker history is not edited directly."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:52.782Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle reconciliation evidence: only pm-pz49xc, pm-ea1yh2, pm-wanwyc, and pm-wa39rl were in progress during this correction round. All implementation and verification evidence is now recorded before the forthcoming close/release mutations, preserving canonical append-only ordering."
  "2026-08-28T05:49:42.112Z","harness:codex","Hosted TDD evidence: graph-composition observed 1,345 prose-edge gaps against the 1,343 ceiling because the lifecycle evidence named the three correction owners without typed edges. Added verifies edges to pm-pz49xc, pm-ea1yh2, and pm-wanwyc; the exact local graph gate must return at or below the ratchet before re-closing."
  "2026-08-28T05:50:05.894Z","harness:codex","Final graph evidence: exact graph-composition passes with 1,342 prose-edge gaps at ceiling 1,343 (explicit 1,215; implicit 127), reducing the hosted failure by three without changing the ratchet or adding generic related edges."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T21:13:28.188Z","harness:codex","A task-level completed boolean is insufficient evidence of successful completion: transcript validity must require a successful terminal step, mutually exclusive refusal metadata, and an explicit recovery_for edge for every retry."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:52.276Z","harness:codex",Append-only lifecycle recovery should create an explicit later work interval and close it in canonical order; never rewrite historical state to hide a prior mismatch.
